  "notes": "USAGE:\n{企|くわだ}てる often implies planning something significant or secretive. The noun form {企|くわだ}て means a plan or scheme. In business contexts, the related word {企画|きかく} (planning, project) is far more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {陰謀|いんぼう}を{企|くわだ}てる (to hatch a conspiracy)\n- クーデターを{企|くわだ}てる (to plot a coup)\n- {暗殺|あんさつ}を{企|くわだ}てる (to plot an assassination)\n- {事業|じぎょう}を{企|くわだ}てる (to plan an enterprise)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {企|くわだ}て: plan, scheme (noun)\n- {企画|きかく}: planning, project\n- {計画|けいかく}する: to plan (neutral)\n- たくらむ: to scheme, to conspire",
